## 3. Crosscheck

### [CXC-CYD-FONT-CROSSCHECK-UPDATE] The crosscheck harness enables atlas mode after canvas construction

- file: cyd/scripts/cyd_dashboard_crosscheck.py
- requirement: immediately after `canvas = SkiaCanvas()`, resolve the atlas path under
  `composeio/render/font_atlas_data.json` and call `canvas.enable_bitmap_atlas(atlas_path)`.
- consequence: every subsequent widget `draw()` routes text through the atlas renderer with no
  per-widget change, because the switch is on the canvas rather than in the widgets.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-FONT-UNIFY]

### [CXC-CYD-FONT-CROSSCHECK-SCREENSHOTS] Crosscheck output is archived as a timestamped progression

- directory: cyd/screenshots/progression/
- artifact-atlas: `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-desktop-atlas.png` — desktop render with the bitmap atlas.
- artifact-native: `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-desktop-native.png` — desktop render with Skia native text, kept for
  comparison.
- artifact-report: `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-comparison-report.txt` — the `pixel_comparison.py` output.
- requirement: copy any CYD captures retrieved from document_store into the same directory, so one
  timestamped set holds every tier's view of the same scene.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-FONT-UNIFY]

