## 4. Acceptance

### [CXC-CYD-FONT-COMPLIANCE] The compliance contract

- definition: seven acceptance criteria, each with the verification that settles it.
- headline-target: the text-area pixel delta drops from 200 to under 10 (FU-C4). That number is the
  whole point of the spec and the one to re-measure if anything here is changed.
- verify-human: the crosscheck PNG and the CYD photograph show text of the same weight, position and
  shape at every size in the scene; a byte-level pass with visibly different text means the comparison
  region is wrong, not that the spec is met.

| ID | Requirement | Verification |
|----|-------------|-------------|
| FU-C1 | `generate_atlas.py` produces both the C header and the JSON from a single invocation | Run the generator; verify both files exist and contain the same glyph count |
| FU-C2 | JSON atlas byte data matches C header byte data for every glyph | Automated comparison: parse both outputs, assert bitmap equality |
| FU-C3 | `BitmapFontAtlas.measure_text()` returns metrics identical to the CYD for all test strings | Unit test with known strings at sizes 8/10/12/14/16 |
| FU-C4 | `SkiaCanvas` with the atlas enabled produces text visually matching the CYD | Pixel comparison: text area delta drops from 200 to under 10 |
| FU-C5 | `SkiaCanvas` without the atlas behaves identically to current behaviour | The existing 122 render engine tests pass unchanged |
| FU-C6 | Nearest-neighbour scaling in Python matches the CYD integer arithmetic | Unit test: render "82C" at size 14 in Python, compare pixel-by-pixel with the CYD atlas reference |
| FU-C7 | Screenshots are saved to `cyd/screenshots/progression/` with timestamps | Verify files created after a crosscheck run |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CYD-FONT-UNIFY]

