**Version**: 1.3 — COMMP is REALIZED on the desktop: fonts.py routes the family and
`COMMP___.TTF` moved cyd/fonts/ -> fonts/ (the one directory the resolver searches), verified to be the
source of the compiled firmware atlas (475 metrics + 435 bitmaps, 0 mismatches).
[CXC-CYD-FONT-FAMILY-ONE-DIRECTORY] and [CXC-CYD-FONT-EXPORT-TOOLCHAIN] added. CORRECTS v1.2, which
declared commp unrealizable on a false claim that the TTF was absent — that claim came from a `find /`
killed at a timeout and read as an empty result. The gap was DISTRIBUTION, not absence.
**Version**: 1.2 — §2b Family routing added ([CXC-CYD-FONT-FAMILY-REGISTRY] / -DEFAULT /
-NO-SILENT-FALLBACK); [CXC-CYD-FONT-RENDERER-INTEGRATE] `behaviour-set-font` corrected (the "family and
weight are ignored" clause was drift — the firmware grew both a bold group and a COMMP family);
[CXC-CYD-FONT-EXPORT] gains `requirement-every-family`. Driven by defect
`font_family: commp` renders IBM Plex Sans on the desktop tier and the COMMP pixel atlas on the device.
**Version**: 1.1 — converted to FactLattice from `cyd/spec/cyd-font-unification.smd` (v1.0, 2026-03-30).
